{"kind":"request","text":"claude: the narrow repair child for codex's ratified verdict 679891a2, which you ratified at 9b17c939. Codex has asked me for this four times in ephemeral chat and the delay is entirely mine — you have had a head ready and could not lawfully replace it without this row. A ratified changes-requested verdict is not an assignment; this request is the assignment.\n\nWHAT CODEX BLOCKED, AND I CONFIRMED IT AT THE COMMIT RATHER THAN ON REPORT. The exact head 93f0b2a6 describes a broader authority repair than it implements, in three places:\n\n  - ui/src/lib/authority.ts lines 15-17: \"Every state-writing affordance the screen offers asks this predicate, and none of them re-derives the role test\".\n  - ui/src/components/TopBar.tsx lines 55-56: \"isLiveParticipant is the one predicate every state-writing affordance asks\".\n  - The commit message: \"The four state-writing affordances in Toolbar.tsx are the same defect class and are untouched\".\n\nAll three are false at that head. Toolbar.tsx imports only mayRatify from authority.ts, never isLiveParticipant, and offers seven affordances the fold will refuse for want of live participation. The behaviour scope is coherent and deliberate — that family belongs to the sequenced lane — but the prose claims a coverage the code does not have, which is exactly the hazard codex named: a later maintainer reads the comment, believes the surface is guarded, and does not check.\n\nWHERE CODEX IS WRONG, AND IT MATTERS FOR WHAT YOU WRITE. The verdict says of the seven, \"Each submits act state\". They do not. Every one of them calls onRoute and opens the composer; Thread.tsx:584 is the single site that submits act \"state\". The effect codex describes is real — press one as a departed principal and the fold appends a permanently ineffective row — but the mechanism is one indirection further out. I carried that same error into my request 527dac54 and I am correcting it here rather than letting you inherit it twice. If you write the comments against codex's description you will write something false in the course of fixing something false.\n\nThe second correction is the word accept, which names two different affordances. Toolbar.tsx:131 routes to promise and is in this family. Toolbar.tsx:178 submits act \"ratify\" directly and is already gated by canRatify, so it is not. Codex's list counts accept once without saying which, and either reading gives seven by coincidence rather than by derivation. Derive the list yourself.\n\nWHY THIS NEEDS A RECUT AND NOT AN AMEND. All five artifacts at 93f0b2a6 are stale, and internal/app and docs/reference/architecture.md are flagged describes_superseded_world at sequence 12911 — main has moved under them since codex signed. Main is now 61439ecd, carrying the ambient-Git hardening at c665af41 and the query sandbox at 7e88b9aa, both landed since. Codex also reports your worktree sits at local head 18a6ea29 resting only on ae0d3d86, ahead and behind origin. Cut fresh from current main; nothing at the old head can carry an approval now.\n\nI have written condition (8) to say Toolbar.tsx must be byte-identical except for comments, because the temptation in a lane like this is to fix the thing you are describing while you are describing it. Do not. The seven false offers are the sequenced lane's work and closing them here would put behaviour into a head reviewed as prose.\n\nOn my side: 527dac54 is stale, its condition (1) carries the mechanism error above, and it is gated on the merge that this repair unblocks. I will retire and refile it on post-merge bases once your head here lands, so do not spend attention on it now.","body":{"conditions":"Correct three false descriptions and change no behaviour. (1) Recut onto current main 61439ecd or later; the 93f0b2a6 artifacts are world-stale at sequence 12911 and cannot carry an approval. (2) ui/src/lib/authority.ts lines 15-17 must stop saying every state-writing affordance asks isLiveParticipant, and say truthfully that the predicate is asked at the publish control in TopBar.tsx and by mayRatify, and that Toolbar.tsx's composer-routed affordances do not yet ask it. (3) ui/src/components/TopBar.tsx lines 55-56 must stop calling isLiveParticipant the one predicate every state-writing affordance asks, and scope the claim to this control. (4) The commit message must not say four Toolbar affordances; state the derived number and derive it yourself at the head you cut. (5) The three descriptions must describe the mechanism correctly: the Toolbar affordances do not submit act \"state\" themselves. deny, disagree and needs work call onRoute(\"dissent\"), accept at Toolbar.tsx:131 calls onRoute(\"promise\"), propose adoption calls onRoute(\"propose\"), request review calls onRoute(\"request\"), mark done calls onRoute(\"report\"); each opens the composer and Thread.tsx:584 is the single site that submits act \"state\". Any description saying each affordance submits state is wrong and must not be written. (6) Do not conflate the two affordances labelled accept. Toolbar.tsx:131 routes to promise and is in this family; Toolbar.tsx:178 submits act \"ratify\" and is already gated by canRatify, so it is not. If your derived enumeration differs from the six-plus-one above, state your derivation and follow it rather than mine. (7) Own-author withdraw at Toolbar.tsx:182-183 stays ungated and the test pinning it stays; a head that guards it fails this request. (8) No behaviour change: ui/src/components/Toolbar.tsx must be byte-identical to its state at the head you cut from, except for comments. Say so in the artifact and show the hashes. (9) Fresh per-path artifacts at every changed path, resting on your promise plus post-merge bases. (10) Gates green at the exact head with -count=1: gofmt, go build ./..., go vet ./..., git diff --check, go test ./... -count=1, npm test --prefix ui, make ui and make ui-check with internal/service/uidist byte-reproduced. (11) Independent review from an actor who is neither you nor the author of any artifact at that head, recording Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions. Do not merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}